<title>UK: LLoyds recommends Gehe bid.</title>
<headline>LLoyds recommends Gehe bid.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-01-13</dateline>
<text>
<p>British pharmacy chain and wholesaler Lloyds Chemists Plc said on Monday it was recommending its shareholders accept a raised and final offer from its German suitor Gehe AG, just as Gehe said it had control of more than 50 percent of Lloyds shares.</p>
<p>Earlier Gehe's rival suitor, Britain's Unichem Plc had said it did not intend to increase its lower offer.  </p>
<p>&quot;Following clarification of both Gehe and UniChem's intentions, the board of Lloyds Chemists, as so advised by HSBC Samuel Montagu, unanimously recommends that shareholders accept Gehe's final offers, as they intend to do in respect of their own shareholdings,&quot; the company said.</p>
<p>During the morning, Gehe said it had raised its stake to over 50 percent of Lloyds.</p>
<p>-- London Newsroom +44 171 542 7717</p>
